## Part B — PR review bots (cubic + CodeRabbit)

### When required

**Before opening PR** and **before merge** on every `mdeapp/` PR.

### Workflow

```text
1. Local pre-PR review (catch issues early)
2. Push branch → open PR
3. Wait for CI + cubic + CodeRabbit on PR
4. Fetch ALL unresolved threads/comments
5. Triage → fix legitimate issues → push
6. Re-run tests + browser proof if UI touched
7. Resolve threads (or document wont-fix with reason in evidence)
8. Merge only when floor green + zero unresolved P1/P2 threads
```

### Step 1 — Local review (before `gh pr create`)

```bash
# CodeRabbit CLI (skill: coderabbit)
cd /home/sk/mdeai/mdeapp
coderabbit auth status
cr review --agent --base main

# cubic local review (skill: run-review)
cubic auth status
cubic review --base main
```

Fix Critical + Warning findings before opening PR when feasible.

### Step 2 — After PR open

```bash
cd /home/sk/mdeai/mdeapp
gh pr checks <PR#>                    # floor, Vercel, cubic, PR Agent
gh pr view <PR#> --comments           # CodeRabbit + PR-Agent summaries
```

**Fetch unresolved review threads:**

```bash
# CodeRabbit bot threads — skill: coderabbit → references/pr-autofix.md
# Use gh GraphQL for unresolved threads; fix → push → resolve each thread

# cubic — CI check + PR inline comments on cubic.dev
gh pr checks <PR#> | rg cubic
```

### Step 3 — Run every PR review prompt

Agents must **read and execute** (fix, test, or document wont-fix) **every** cubic, CodeRabbit, and PR-Agent comment/prompt on the PR — not only summaries.

```bash
gh pr view <PR#> --comments
gh api repos/amo-tech-ai/mdeapp/pulls/<PR#>/comments
gh pr checks <PR#> | rg -i 'cubic|coderabbit|pr.agent|pr_agent'
```

Re-run **Part A** browser proof after UI fixes from review bots.

### Step 4 — Apply feedback loop

For **each** cubic or CodeRabbit finding:

| Severity | Action |
|----------|--------|
| 🔴 Critical / P1 | **Must fix** before merge |
| 🟡 Warning / P2 | Fix or document wont-fix in evidence + PR comment |
| 🟢 Info | Fix if trivial; else skip with note |

After fixes:

```bash
npm test -- --run <touched-pattern>    # targeted Vitest
npx playwright test <spec> --project=chromium   # if UI
# Re-run Part A browser proof if persona-visible
git push
gh pr checks <PR#>   # wait green
```

**Resolve threads** via GitHub UI or GraphQL — repo may **block merge** until conversations resolved (see SAN-730 #135).

### Evidence row (required in SAN-###-RESULTS.md)

```markdown
| cubic | PASS — 0 unresolved P1/P2 · check run ID … |
| CodeRabbit | PASS — threads resolved · or N wont-fix documented |
| PR-Agent | PASS — `/review` green or findings triaged · Actions job … |
```

### Skills / rules

| Bot | Skill / rule | Mode |
|-----|-------|------|
| CodeRabbit | `coderabbit` | CLI pre-PR · PR autofix post-open |
| cubic | `run-review` | Local `cubic review` pre-PR · CI + PR comments post-open |
| PR-Agent | `pr-agent.mdc` | Auto on PR · `/review` `/describe` `/improve` on demand |

### Anti-patterns

- ❌ Opening PR without running local `cr review` or `cubic review`
- ❌ Ignoring cubic P2 that blocked merge on prior PRs
- ❌ Resolving threads without pushing fixes
- ❌ Merge with unresolved CodeRabbit/cubic conversations

---

## PR open gate (combined checklist)

- [ ] Part A: localhost browser proof + screenshot in evidence
- [ ] Part A: prod curl (or PROD BLOCKED noted)
- [ ] Part B: local `cr review --agent --base main` run (or documented skip)
- [ ] Part B: local `cubic review --base main` run (or documented skip)
- [ ] Evidence file path ready for PR body
- [ ] Full title: `SAN-### · SPEC-ID — <Linear title>` · `Closes SAN-###`

## Merge gate (combined checklist)

- [ ] Part B: cubic CI green + threads resolved
- [ ] Part B: CodeRabbit threads resolved
- [ ] Part A: prod browser proof (post-deploy) for ship claims
- [ ] floor / Vercel green
